  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef la_eigendecomposition(A: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Eigendecomposition** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef la_eigendecomposition(A: list) -> dict:\n    vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(np.array(A, dtype=float))\n    idx = np.argsort(vals)[::-1]\n    return {'eigenvalues': np.round(vals[idx], 4).tolist(), 'eigenvectors': np.round(vecs[:, idx], 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
